Builds FastPFOR's bit-width helper without x86 assembly on every target but
x86. The helper falls back to x86's `bsr` instruction on any architecture it
does not list, so mlt-cpp fails to compile for RISC-V and LoongArch. The
portable builtin it already uses on ARM and WebAssembly serves them too.
Upstream: not proposed

